put.description:
Write-only. The value goes straight into the environment's region (<workload>-secret-env);
RunR keeps the name, a version and a keyed fingerprint (503 when the region does not answer:
nothing changed).

post.description:
Needs a ready Knative Operator; runs as a background job. A Serving that already runs in the
namespace is adopted instead. `version` is a Knative minor of GET …/compatible-versions;
without it, the newest the cluster supports and the operator can install.

stopped.description:
Stopped by an administrator (POST /projects/{project}/stop): shown to every member;
level "platform" (a platform administrator — only one can resume it) or "organization";
system "cost_limit" when RunR stopped it by itself (ProjectStopService::stopBySystem)
